{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40608","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46290","text":"Graphonomous × box-and-box — Arithmetic Compliance Review"}]},{"id":"blk-40609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46291","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-46292","text":" review (no behavior change) · "},{"id":"spn-46293","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-46294","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46295","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-46296","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-46297","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-46298","text":" how closely the Graphonomous memory engine (OS-001) already conforms to the [&] governance kernel, rung by rung, and the small set of *additive* naming/wiring changes that would make it explicitly compliant."}]},{"id":"blk-40610","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46299","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-40611","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46300","text":"Graphonomous is "},{"id":"spn-46301","marks":["bold"],"text":"already structurally isomorphic"},{"id":"spn-46302","text":" to the kernel's load-bearing rungs — it just doesn't *name* them. Its coverage→decision policy is the bridge ("},{"id":"spn-46303","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-46304","text":"); its coverage score is the axiological semiring; its Wilson intervals are the epistemic rung; its cost cap is the resource rung's affine ledger. The gap is "},{"id":"spn-46305","marks":["bold"],"text":"vocabulary + two small guarantees"},{"id":"spn-46306","text":", not architecture. Nothing here requires a core refactor; every recommendation is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-40612","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46307","text":"Compliance scorecard"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40614","spans":[{"id":"spn-46308","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-40615","spans":[{"id":"spn-46309","text":"Graphonomous implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-40616","spans":[{"id":"spn-46310","text":"Compliance"}]}],"id":"blk-40613","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40617","spans":[{"id":"spn-46311","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-46312","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-46313","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-40618","spans":[{"id":"spn-46314","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology.compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-46315","text":", SCC analysis; node confidence"}]},{"id":"blk-40619","spans":[{"id":"spn-46316","text":"✅ ~90% — κ is a first-class Value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40620","spans":[{"id":"spn-46317","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-46318","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-46319","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-40621","spans":[{"id":"spn-46320","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-46321","text":", "},{"id":"spn-46322","marks":["code"],"text":"Reranker"}]},{"id":"blk-40622","spans":[{"id":"spn-46323","text":"◻ ~60% — weighted sum, not a *named* semiring"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40623","spans":[{"id":"spn-46324","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-40624","spans":[{"id":"spn-46325","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-46326","text":" floor gates (act/learn/escalate)"}]},{"id":"blk-40625","spans":[{"id":"spn-46327","text":"◻ ~70% — floor present, "},{"id":"spn-46328","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-46329","text":" veto implicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40626","spans":[{"id":"spn-46330","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-40627","spans":[{"id":"spn-46331","text":"consolidation cadence; freshness/staleness decay"}]},{"id":"blk-40628","spans":[{"id":"spn-46332","text":"◻ ~40% — time-aware, no LTL obligations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40629","spans":[{"id":"spn-46333","text":"5. reflexive (entrenched ring-0)"}]},{"id":"blk-40630","spans":[{"id":"spn-46334","text":"— (no self-amendment surface)"}]},{"id":"blk-40631","spans":[{"id":"spn-46335","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40632","spans":[{"id":"spn-46336","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-40633","spans":[{"id":"spn-46337","marks":["code"],"text":"Uncertainty.interval/1"},{"id":"spn-46338","text":" (Wilson), "},{"id":"spn-46339","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-46340","text":" (AGM)"}]},{"id":"blk-40634","spans":[{"id":"spn-46341","text":"✅ ~95% — strongest rung"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40635","spans":[{"id":"spn-46342","text":"7. strategic (coalition power)"}]},{"id":"blk-40636","spans":[{"id":"spn-46343","text":"— (single-agent; delegated to Deliberatic)"}]},{"id":"blk-40637","spans":[{"id":"spn-46344","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40638","spans":[{"id":"spn-46345","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-40639","spans":[{"id":"spn-46346","marks":["code"],"text":"CostTracker.budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-46347","text":" ($10/day), "},{"id":"spn-46348","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-46349","text":" LRU+decay"}]},{"id":"blk-40640","spans":[{"id":"spn-46350","text":"◻ ~85% — ledger present"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40641","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46351","text":"Rung-by-rung detail (grounded in the code)"}]},{"id":"blk-40642","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46352","text":"Rung 1 — alethic ("},{"id":"spn-46353","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-46354","text":") ✅"}]},{"id":"blk-40643","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46355","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/topology.ex"},{"id":"spn-46356","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46357","marks":["code"],"text":"compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-46358","text":" (line 134) computes the "},{"id":"spn-46359","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ cyclicity invariant"},{"id":"spn-46360","text":" — the same Value-family invariant the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-46361","marks":["code"],"text":"value.mjs"},{"id":"spn-46362","text":" carries (alethic \"what can happen\"). Node confidence scores are the truth-degrees over which Value laws "},{"id":"spn-46363","marks":["code"],"text":"L1–L14"},{"id":"spn-46364","text":" range. "},{"id":"spn-46365","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-46366","text":"; recommend citing the rung-1 correspondence in the "},{"id":"spn-46367","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology"},{"id":"spn-46368","text":" moduledoc so κ is understood as the alethic Value, not a bespoke metric."}]},{"id":"blk-40644","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46369","text":"Rung 2 — axiological ("},{"id":"spn-46370","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-46371","text":") ◻ → name the semiring"}]},{"id":"blk-40645","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46372","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-46373","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46374","marks":["code"],"text":"weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-46375","text":" (line 604) computes "},{"id":"spn-46376","marks":["code"],"text":"Σ value × weight"},{"id":"spn-46377","text":" and clamps to "},{"id":"spn-46378","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,1]"},{"id":"spn-46379","text":". That is the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-46380","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability semiring"},{"id":"spn-46381","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-46382","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = +"},{"id":"spn-46383","text":", "},{"id":"spn-46384","marks":["code"],"text":"⊗ = ×"},{"id":"spn-46385","text":") from "},{"id":"spn-46386","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-46387","text":". "},{"id":"spn-46388","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-46389","text":" document that the coverage score *is* the axiological rung in the probability semiring, and (optionally) expose a tropical ("},{"id":"spn-46390","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = min"},{"id":"spn-46391","text":") \"weakest-component\" view alongside the weighted mean — so the engine can answer \"is any coverage component failing?\" the way the kernel's safety floor does, not just \"how good on average?\"."}]},{"id":"blk-40646","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46392","text":"Rung 3 — deontic (norm/govern) ◻ → make the "},{"id":"spn-46393","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-46394","text":" veto explicit"}]},{"id":"blk-40647","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46395","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-46396","text":" (line 392) is "},{"id":"spn-46397","marks":["bold"],"text":"the bridge, already implemented"},{"id":"spn-46398","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-40648","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":act  when coverage ≥ floor  AND uncertainty ≤ ceiling  AND risk ≤ ceiling   # feasible ▸ permitted\n:learn when (looser floor)                                                    # permitted, not yet best\n:escalate otherwise                                                           # floor not met"},{"id":"blk-40649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46399","text":"This is exactly "},{"id":"spn-46400","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-46401","text":": the conjunctive thresholds are the "},{"id":"spn-46402","marks":["bold"],"text":"un-weakenable safety floor"},{"id":"spn-46403","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-46404","marks":["code"],"text":"decision_confidence/3"},{"id":"spn-46405","text":" (line 409) is the "},{"id":"spn-46406","marks":["bold"],"text":"gradient"},{"id":"spn-46407","text":" that the bridge's "},{"id":"spn-46408","marks":["code"],"text":"best"},{"id":"spn-46409","text":" step optimizes. The one missing guarantee is "},{"id":"spn-46410","marks":["bold"],"text":"`0̲` annihilation"},{"id":"spn-46411","text":": in the kernel, a floor violation *annihilates* the verdict (no amount of gradient can rescue it). Graphonomous approximates this — "},{"id":"spn-46412","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-46413","text":" is terminal — but the relationship is implicit. "},{"id":"spn-46414","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-46415","text":" state in the "},{"id":"spn-46416","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage"},{"id":"spn-46417","text":" moduledoc that a sub-floor signal annihilates to "},{"id":"spn-46418","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-46419","text":" (the deontic "},{"id":"spn-46420","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-46421","text":"), and add a property test mirroring the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-46422","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-46423","text":" annihilation law so the guarantee can't silently regress."}]},{"id":"blk-40650","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46424","text":"Rung 4 — temporal (LTL ▸ supervise) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-40651","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46425","text":"Freshness/staleness decay ("},{"id":"spn-46426","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-46427","text":" line 383) and consolidation cadence are time-aware, but there are no explicit LTL obligations (e.g. \"every stored contradiction is *eventually* resolved\"). "},{"id":"spn-46428","marks":["bold"],"text":"Out of scope to add now"},{"id":"spn-46429","text":"; flagged as the natural next rung if temporal guarantees become first-class. Maps to "},{"id":"spn-46430","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/temporal.mjs"},{"id":"spn-46431","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-46432","marks":["code"],"text":"X"},{"id":"spn-46433","text":", "},{"id":"spn-46434","marks":["code"],"text":"◇"},{"id":"spn-46435","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-40652","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46436","text":"Rung 6 — epistemic (knows ▸ believes) ✅ strongest"}]},{"id":"blk-40653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46437","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/uncertainty.ex"},{"id":"spn-46438","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46439","marks":["code"],"text":"interval/1"},{"id":"spn-46440","text":" (line 28) computes "},{"id":"spn-46441","marks":["bold"],"text":"Wilson confidence intervals"},{"id":"spn-46442","text":" over evidence counts, with an explicit "},{"id":"spn-46443","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-46444","text":" bottom — this is the kernel's epistemic rung (S5/KD45 \"knows ▸ believes\") in statistical form. "},{"id":"spn-46445","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-46446","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-46447","marks":["bold"],"text":"AGM"},{"id":"spn-46448","text":" expansion/contraction with "},{"id":"spn-46449","marks":["code"],"text":"contradicts"},{"id":"spn-46450","text":" edges. "},{"id":"spn-46451","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-46452","text":" at ~95%; recommend naming the "},{"id":"spn-46453","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-46454","text":" case as the epistemic bottom and citing the rung-6 correspondence. This is the rung Graphonomous could claim conformance on today."}]},{"id":"blk-40654","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46455","text":"Rung 8 — resource (affine ledger) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-40655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46456","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/cost_tracker.ex"},{"id":"spn-46457","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46458","marks":["code"],"text":"budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-46459","text":" (line 167) enforces a "},{"id":"spn-46460","marks":["code"],"text":"$10/day"},{"id":"spn-46461","text":" cap — an "},{"id":"spn-46462","marks":["bold"],"text":"affine ledger"},{"id":"spn-46463","text":": spend is consumed and cannot go negative past the cap. The "},{"id":"spn-46464","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-46465","text":" (LRU + priority decay) is resource reclamation. This is the kernel's resource rung ("},{"id":"spn-46466","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-46467","text":", laws "},{"id":"spn-46468","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-46469","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-46470","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-46471","text":" emit the daily-budget remaining as a resource signal and name it with the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-46472","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-46473","text":", overspend → "},{"id":"spn-46474","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-46475","text":"), so unattended autonomy degrades gracefully via the same algebra the kernel uses."}]},{"id":"blk-40656","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46476","text":"Recommended changes (all additive, no behavior change)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40658","spans":[{"id":"spn-46477","text":"Change"}]},{"id":"blk-40659","spans":[{"id":"spn-46478","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-40660","spans":[{"id":"spn-46479","text":"Risk"}]},{"id":"blk-40661","spans":[{"id":"spn-46480","text":"Value"}]}],"id":"blk-40657","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40662","spans":[{"id":"spn-46481","text":"Cite κ = alethic Value"}]},{"id":"blk-40663","spans":[{"id":"spn-46482","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.ex"},{"id":"spn-46483","text":" moduledoc"}]},{"id":"blk-40664","spans":[{"id":"spn-46484","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-40665","spans":[{"id":"spn-46485","text":"shared vocabulary"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40666","spans":[{"id":"spn-46486","text":"Name coverage score = probability semiring; optional tropical view"}]},{"id":"blk-40667","spans":[{"id":"spn-46487","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage.ex"}]},{"id":"blk-40668","spans":[{"id":"spn-46488","text":"low"}]},{"id":"blk-40669","spans":[{"id":"spn-46489","text":"bottleneck visibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40670","spans":[{"id":"spn-46490","text":"State the "},{"id":"spn-46491","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-46492","text":" annihilation on sub-floor; add "},{"id":"spn-46493","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-46494","text":"-style property test"}]},{"id":"blk-40671","spans":[{"id":"spn-46495","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-46496","text":" + test"}]},{"id":"blk-40672","spans":[{"id":"spn-46497","text":"low"}]},{"id":"blk-40673","spans":[{"id":"spn-46498","text":"regression guard"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40674","spans":[{"id":"spn-46499","text":"Name Wilson "},{"id":"spn-46500","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-46501","text":" as epistemic bottom"}]},{"id":"blk-40675","spans":[{"id":"spn-46502","marks":["code"],"text":"uncertainty.ex"},{"id":"spn-46503","text":" moduledoc"}]},{"id":"blk-40676","spans":[{"id":"spn-46504","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-40677","spans":[{"id":"spn-46505","text":"claim rung-6 conformance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40678","spans":[{"id":"spn-46506","text":"Emit resource-ledger remaining with kernel vocabulary"}]},{"id":"blk-40679","spans":[{"id":"spn-46507","marks":["code"],"text":"cost_tracker.ex"}]},{"id":"blk-40680","spans":[{"id":"spn-46508","text":"low"}]},{"id":"blk-40681","spans":[{"id":"spn-46509","text":"graceful autonomy"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40682","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46510","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-40683","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40685","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46511","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-46512","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-46513","text":" change any decision thresholds, coverage weights, or confidence formulas."}]}],"id":"blk-40684","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40687","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46514","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-46515","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-46516","text":" make Graphonomous call the JS kernel at runtime — Graphonomous stays"}]}],"id":"blk-40686","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46517","text":"self-contained Elixir; the kernel is the *specification* its algebra conforms to."}]},{"id":"blk-40689","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46518","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-46519","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-46520","text":" add the reflexive (rung 5) or strategic (rung 7) rungs — those are"}]}],"id":"blk-40690","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40692","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46521","text":"single-agent-out-of-scope and delegated to Delegatic/Deliberatic respectively."}]},{"id":"blk-40693","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46522","text":"Reference"}]},{"id":"blk-40694","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"b